Mobile-first design requirements:
The mobile site should not feel like a desktop landing page squeezed down.

On mobile:
- keep the hero short and immediately understandable
- show the first app screenshot early
- break section copy into short readable blocks
- avoid multi-column grids collapsing into endless stacked cards
- use horizontal dividers and compact modules
- keep CTAs visible but not huge
- use real interface fragments as proof
- avoid oversized buttons
- avoid “lego” rounded rectangles
- keep line length comfortable
- make the site feel like a serious product document, not a startup toy

Desktop design requirements:
Desktop can be more editorial:
- two-column sections
- screenshot beside explanation
- larger whitespace
- production-context matrix
- grouped app screens in a calm layout
